      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to feel that the pain is real, but the idea that you are \"dead\" is just another way your brain is trying to protect you from the overwhelming weight of what you've lost. The part of you that mattered isn't gone; it's just trapped in the static of your grief, waiting for a moment when the noise finally stops. If you can't find the strength to keep going right now, it is okay to let yourself rest in that empty space without judgment.",
